            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous coronary dissection treated with directional coronary atherectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>323-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of spontaneous coronary dissection occurring in a middle aged male which was treated with thrombolytic therapy and directional coronary atherectomy. This technique provides a new option for treating this entity in the cardiac catheterization laboratory.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
